  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "One server, one catalog",
      "items": [
        "The page and the chat's MCP server both go through the same HTTP API (core/mcp_bridge.py), so a change from either shows in the other",
        "Listing, hashing, publishing and scans run as jobs, one at a time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What stays on the PC",
      "items": [
        "Face and pet crops, embeddings, look vectors and extracted text stay in the catalog and the workspace",
        "Models run on the CPU through ONNX Runtime; first start fetches them with pinned SHA-256s",
        "The server listens on 127.0.0.1 only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "The chat",
      "items": [
        "Claude Code under the person's own claude.ai account: no API key, no shell, no files, no web",
        "It sees only this edge's MCP tools, and every change it asks for waits for a Confirm"
      ]
    }
  ]
